        <name>get_buffer</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Retrieves a pointer to the tensor&apos;s buffer. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function provides access to the buffer that was provided during tensor construction.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>void* Pointer to the buffer, or nullptr if no buffer is available or if the tensor was constructed with a const buffer. If the memory type is <ref refid="namespacevart_1a628146123b56321d35a9614480f55cb4aa6a383cd83e54008ecd424550f46c74f" kindref="member">MemoryType::XRT_BO</ref>, it returns a pointer to the corresponding xrt::bo. If the memory type is <ref refid="namespacevart_1a628146123b56321d35a9614480f55cb4a2dfccb788ee18c89a3a4872ee1c054d3" kindref="member">MemoryType::DMA_FD</ref>, it returns a pointer to the file descriptor. For <ref refid="namespacevart_1a628146123b56321d35a9614480f55cb4afd8b57da11def05c5970111166f627bb" kindref="member">MemoryType::USER_POINTER_CMA</ref> and <ref refid="namespacevart_1a628146123b56321d35a9614480f55cb4a22fe977dbb4918ca8ae60b4e945594ba" kindref="member">MemoryType::USER_POINTER_NON_CMA</ref>, it returns the virtual pointer. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Returns nullptr for tensors constructed with const void* buffer. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
